    {
      "seq": 24,
      "kind": "submit",
      "at": 1791673403545,
      "reason": "BasicTokenizer.encode on long inputs (>=256 bytes): when the merges satisfy the trained-merge invariant (distinct int idx, each idx greater than both tokens of its pair, all below 0x110000; checked on every call, otherwise falls back to apply_merges), lowest-idx-first merging is equivalent to applying str.replace for each pair in increasing idx order on a latin-1 string of ids. A merge only creates pairs containing the new idx, which have a higher idx, and str.replace matches left to right without overlaps like merge(). This replaces the Python heap loop with C string replaces. Equivalence identical; encode_ir -1.70%."
    }
  ],
